# What must never enter the build context.
#
# Without this file, `docker build` uploads everything in the directory to the
# daemon — including a local .env and a 200 MB node_modules built for the wrong
# platform. The .env line is the one that matters: a secret that reaches the
# build context can end up in an image layer, and an image layer is forever.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules/
npm-debug.log*

.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# The tests and the contract fixtures are not part of the running service.
test/
contract/

*.md
!README.md

.DS_Store
coverage/
